Real towns, built from OpenStreetMap, playable in Project Zomboid Build 42. Each town was made with Portal, a free, unofficial Windows app that turns any real place into a map mod. The map building is done by KnoxMap by euclid80tr.

This collection holds the towns and the small [b]Portal[/b] companion mod. The companion mod adds a Portal button to the main menu that lists your installed Portal towns and explains how to make your own. It is optional; every town works without it.

Enable only one Portal town at a time. They share the same spot in the world.

Make your own town: [url=https://github.com/derpasaurus69-crypto/zomboidmods/releases]https://github.com/derpasaurus69-crypto/zomboidmods/releases[/url]

Tested in singleplayer on one Windows PC. Multiplayer has not been tested.

